        "title": "How to read this",
        "vizConfig": {
          "group": "text",
          "kind": "VizConfig",
          "spec": {
            "fieldConfig": {
              "defaults": {},
              "overrides": []
            },
            "options": {
              "mode": "markdown",
              "content": "### How to read this dashboard\n\nUse the **Ticker** selector (top-left) to pick one or more stocks/ETFs — every panel scopes to the selection and the time picker.\n\n**Hit rate = CORRECT ÷ (CORRECT + INCORRECT)** at the **30-day** horizon (the long-term headline metric); *neutral calls are excluded*, so a single ticker often has a small sample — check *Decided calls* before trusting the rate.\n\n- The **price history** starts 2026-06-12 (when in-repo daily price collection began). Orange markers flag **action flips** (the call changed vs the previous run) — hover for old → new action; unchanged daily calls are not marked.\n- **Hit rate by horizon** fills in as outcomes mature (first 90d ≈ Oct 2026, first 1y ≈ May 2027); grading bands widen with the horizon (a 1-year BUY must beat +15%, not +4%).\n- **avg return %** is the mean forward return of graded calls — direction-blind (a correct SELL can coexist with a positive underlying return).\n- The **call history** table shows every call in range with its 30-day grade (empty verdict = not matured yet or no exit price).",
              "code": {
                "language": "plaintext",
                "showLineNumbers": false,
                "showMiniMap": false
              }
            }
          },
          "version": "13.2.0-28852654685"
        }
      }
    },
    "panel-5": {
      "kind": "Panel",
      "spec": {
